1
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
With your heart, truly see

2
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,000
The truth is right nearby

3
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Hey you good or bad, real or fake

4
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,000
You can't escape this soul's gray haze

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Take all the courage you own

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Maybe you can save this world

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

8
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

9
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Mojo Mojo Mojo Spy

10
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:17,000
In the previous episode, to investigate the Illumin-Eye, Hawxing went to the Whitewater Pond Nature Reserve.

11
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:18,000
The reserve's golden monkeys were attacked by the hunter, Storm.

12
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,000
And the mastermind behind it all, Dorothy, seemed to have an even more terrifying plan.

13
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,200
Tantalus.

14
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,760
On such a crisp and clear day

15
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:32,340
It's so perfect for a trip out

16
00:01:32,340 --> 00:01:34,519
Now, a news bulletin.

17
00:01:34,519 --> 00:01:35,420
Dear viewers,

18
00:01:35,420 --> 00:01:36,659
We interrupt with breaking news.

19
00:01:36,659 --> 00:01:39,439
Today in the Whitewater Pond Nature Reserve,

20
00:01:39,439 --> 00:01:40,739
a golden monkey

21
00:01:40,739 --> 00:01:42,599
bizarrely turned into a piece of amber.

22
00:01:42,599 --> 00:01:50,200
Golden monkeys are rare animals in the Whitewater Pond Nature Reserve.

23
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:51,859
The cause of the golden monkey's mutation

24
00:01:51,859 --> 00:01:53,159
is under investigation.

25
00:01:53,159 --> 00:01:55,480
We initially suspect it was man-made.

26
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:57,480
Citizens, rest assured

27
00:01:57,480 --> 00:02:02,480
I, Inspector Sima, will bring those criminals to justice

28
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:09,480
For the people's interests!

29
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:16,480
That's all for this news bulletin

30
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:19,480
May the golden monkeys recover soon

31
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:21,480
Goodbye!

32
00:02:25,479 --> 00:02:28,039
Uncle, uncle!

33
00:02:28,039 --> 00:02:29,280
Something big happened!

34
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:44,659
Officer Han

35
00:02:44,659 --> 00:02:45,379
How's the situation?

36
00:02:45,379 --> 00:02:47,539
No progress yet

37
00:02:47,539 --> 00:02:50,060
But earlier, we received

38
00:02:50,060 --> 00:02:51,299
intelligence from Hawxing

39
00:02:51,299 --> 00:02:52,739
This might be the

40
00:02:52,739 --> 00:02:53,839
Illumin-Eye's doing again

41
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:55,920
But until we figure out

42
00:02:55,920 --> 00:02:57,259
their true intention

43
00:02:57,259 --> 00:02:59,120
we can only use limited manpower

44
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:01,460
to keep a close watch on the monkeys in the reserve

45
00:03:01,460 --> 00:03:04,140
Little monkey

46
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:05,659
Where is the little monkey?

47
00:03:05,659 --> 00:03:06,939
Is it alright?

48
00:03:06,939 --> 00:03:09,159
Well... how do I put this?

49
00:03:09,159 --> 00:03:10,420
Let Inspector Sima

50
00:03:10,420 --> 00:03:12,840
take you to Dr. Breeze's lab to see

51
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:35,259
Dr. Breeze

52
00:03:35,259 --> 00:03:37,960
Sorry to bother you.

53
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:41,980
Inspector Sima

54
00:03:41,980 --> 00:03:44,020
Come in, come in.

55
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:46,280
I've been knocking on the door for ages.

56
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:48,360
I thought you were still resting.

57
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:50,840
Sorry.

58
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:54,280
Maybe I was too focused on crunching the numbers.

59
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:55,900
I didn't hear you knock.

60
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:59,340
So, may I ask who these are?

61
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:01,259
Let me introduce.

62
00:04:01,259 --> 00:04:03,580
This is the famous detective, Jimmy Chen.

63
00:04:03,580 --> 00:04:05,840
This is the little detective, Locky.

64
00:04:05,840 --> 00:04:07,980
Jingjing and Hawxing

65
00:04:07,980 --> 00:04:12,340
They're all Officer Han.

66
00:04:12,340 --> 00:04:13,860
Brought in to help solve the case.

67
00:04:13,860 --> 00:04:16,420
This is the one stationed at

68
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:17,660
Whitewater Pond Nature Reserve

69
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:19,639
Dr. Breeze, who does animal research

70
00:04:19,639 --> 00:04:23,939
He's also the one in charge of researching this golden monkey mutation.

71
00:04:23,939 --> 00:04:27,539
Welcome, detectives!

72
00:04:27,539 --> 00:04:29,439
That was really rude of me just now.

73
00:04:29,439 --> 00:04:31,379
Hello, Doctor.

74
00:04:31,379 --> 00:04:35,860
I'd like to know how the research on the mutant snub-nosed monkeys is going.

75
00:04:35,860 --> 00:04:40,240
To figure out this strange mutation.

76
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:42,800
I've consulted a ton of material.

77
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:46,419
I've asked world-famous zoologists, too.

78
00:04:46,419 --> 00:04:48,579
But still, nothing.

79
00:04:48,579 --> 00:04:50,359
Based on initial research,

80
00:04:50,359 --> 00:04:54,379
the golden snub-nosed monkey was hit by some kind of external energy blast,

81
00:04:54,379 --> 00:04:56,479
which caused its body to mutate

82
00:04:56,479 --> 00:04:59,659
into this amber-like form.

83
00:04:59,659 --> 00:05:01,599
And here's the kicker—

84
00:05:01,599 --> 00:05:03,839
even though the monkey's like this now,

85
00:05:03,839 --> 00:05:06,060
its life hasn't stopped.

86
00:05:06,060 --> 00:05:07,079
Its heartbeat,

87
00:05:07,079 --> 00:05:09,959
blood circulation, everything—

88
00:05:09,959 --> 00:05:12,039
all still going.

89
00:05:12,039 --> 00:05:12,459
Ugh.

90
00:05:12,459 --> 00:05:13,779
With no other choice,

91
00:05:13,779 --> 00:05:15,199
right now,

92
00:05:15,199 --> 00:05:19,399
I can only use a special culture tank to keep it alive.

93
00:05:19,399 --> 00:05:21,240
Doctor,

94
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:24,620
why connect those two big tanks together?

95
00:05:24,620 --> 00:05:27,579
If the nutrient solution exceeds the organism itself,

96
00:05:27,579 --> 00:05:29,560
the organism in the tank dies.

97
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:31,800
So I linked the two tanks—

98
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:35,199
the extra solution automatically flows into the other one.

99
00:05:35,199 --> 00:05:37,199
Clever.

100
00:05:37,959 --> 00:05:43,199
But that won't turn the monkey back to normal.

101
00:05:43,199 --> 00:05:45,439
It's all because I'm so useless.

102
00:05:45,439 --> 00:05:46,979
I studied medicine for so many years,

103
00:05:46,979 --> 00:05:50,199
but in the end, I couldn't save even one little life.

104
00:05:50,199 --> 00:05:56,560
That poor little monkey.

105
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:59,079
It really is so pitiful.

106
00:05:59,079 --> 00:06:03,039
Doctor, don't worry. There'll be a way.

107
00:06:03,039 --> 00:06:05,000
Everyone—oh, Dr. Breeze!

108
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,959
Didn't you tell me last night you had a new clue?

109
00:06:07,959 --> 00:06:11,300
Doctor, have you found other clues?

110
00:06:11,300 --> 00:06:14,639
Well, how should I put it?

111
00:06:14,639 --> 00:06:16,620
Rather than a clue,

112
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:19,439
it's more like my own wild imagination.

113
00:06:19,439 --> 00:06:24,860
Do you know the story of Tantalus?

114
00:06:24,860 --> 00:06:28,759
You mean Tantalus from Greek mythology?

115
00:06:28,759 --> 00:06:31,100
What does that have to do with the little monkey?

116
00:06:31,100 --> 00:06:32,060
Uncle,

117
00:06:32,060 --> 00:06:34,759
can you tell us the story of Tantalus?

118
00:06:34,759 --> 00:06:40,120
Tantalus, in Greek mythology,

119
00:06:40,120 --> 00:06:41,579
was the son of Zeus, the king of gods.

120
00:06:41,579 --> 00:06:44,240
At first, the gods showered him with favor.

121
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:48,060
But because of it, he grew proud and arrogant.

122
00:06:48,060 --> 00:06:51,240
He even began to brazenly insult the gods.

123
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:54,899
In the end, the enraged gods cast him into the underworld.

124
00:06:54,899 --> 00:06:58,039
In a pool of deep water,

125
00:06:58,279 --> 00:07:00,539
the waves pressed against his thirsty...

126
00:07:00,539 --> 00:07:02,740
Tantalus' chest churned.

127
00:07:02,740 --> 00:07:05,519
When he bent down to drink,

128
00:07:05,519 --> 00:07:08,780
the water instantly flowed away from him,

129
00:07:08,780 --> 00:07:11,120
leaving him standing empty-handed

130
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:13,480
on a tiny ledge that could hardly support him.

131
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:15,720
Branches bent low with fruit

132
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:18,220
hung before famished Tantalus.

133
00:07:18,220 --> 00:07:21,079
If he stood on tiptoe to take them,

134
00:07:21,079 --> 00:07:23,680
a gust of wind would sweep down from the sky,

135
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:26,240
blowing the branches high into the air,

136
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:27,540
keeping them forever out of reach.

137
00:07:27,540 --> 00:07:31,120
A giant rock hung over Tantalus' head.

138
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:32,780
If it moved even a little,

139
00:07:32,780 --> 00:07:34,379
it would come crashing down,

140
00:07:34,379 --> 00:07:35,860
smashing him to pieces.

141
00:07:35,860 --> 00:07:38,620
Later, people often used Tantalus' name

142
00:07:38,620 --> 00:07:40,240
to describe a person in torment,

143
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:41,980
and Tantalus' misery

144
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:44,379
to describe the pain of seeing your goal

145
00:07:44,379 --> 00:07:47,399
but never reaching it.

146
00:07:47,399 --> 00:07:54,160
Don't you think the mutant golden monkey's situation

147
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:56,939
is just like Tantalus' curse?

148
00:07:56,939 --> 00:08:00,000
It does seem somewhat similar.

149
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:03,519
But how does that help the mutant golden monkey?

150
00:08:03,519 --> 00:08:05,660
I really can't wrap my head around it.

151
00:08:14,699 --> 00:08:15,300
The light it gives off is so beautiful, so beautiful.

152
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:17,079
Yeah, yeah.

153
00:08:17,079 --> 00:08:18,720
Feeling enveloped by this glow,

154
00:08:18,720 --> 00:08:20,800
my mood has become cheerful too.

155
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:23,160
This is a twin necklace passed down in my family.

156
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:25,079
It's called the Pendant of Tantalus.

157
00:08:25,079 --> 00:08:29,360
The harmonious light it emits

158
00:08:29,360 --> 00:08:33,840
can make people's hearts feel calm and peaceful.

159
00:08:43,799 --> 00:08:44,120
The twin necklace is made of a strange metal.

160
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:48,800
Its properties are exactly opposite to those of the mutated golden monkeys.

161
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:50,200
Yes.

162
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:53,759
I've also studied the properties of both.

163
00:08:53,980 --> 00:08:55,759
Just as you said,

164
00:08:55,759 --> 00:08:58,759
their properties are exactly contradictory to each other.

165
00:08:58,759 --> 00:09:03,580
After that, I began experimenting with the necklace to help the golden monkeys recover.

166
00:09:03,580 --> 00:09:06,240
But the results were still fruitless.

167
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:10,779
Doctor, you just said this is a twin necklace,

168
00:09:10,779 --> 00:09:13,960
so where is the other one?

169
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:17,240
The other pendant of Tantalus

170
00:09:17,240 --> 00:09:21,319
is worn by my twin brother, Storm.

171
00:09:21,319 --> 00:09:24,919
Wow, so there's another necklace.

172
00:09:24,919 --> 00:09:27,679
Is the other one just as beautiful?

173
00:09:27,680 --> 00:09:30,080
Mm, my brother Storm's necklace

174
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:32,460
is basically the same shape as mine,

175
00:09:32,460 --> 00:09:35,300
but his necklace gives off...

176
00:09:35,300 --> 00:09:36,580
Like a black hole

177
00:09:36,580 --> 00:09:39,120
A force that devours all light

178
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:41,260
Maybe because of the

179
00:09:41,260 --> 00:09:43,000
influence of the necklace he wears

180
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,960
Storm was a mischievous kid

181
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:47,800
Giving everyone a headache

182
00:09:47,800 --> 00:09:50,080
I haven't seen him in years

183
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:51,920
And now I don't even know

184
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:53,780
Where my no-good brother

185
00:09:53,780 --> 00:09:55,420
has gone

186
00:09:57,680 --> 00:10:04,560
I really don't want to be alone and lonely

187
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:12,480
Life always has some unhappy moments

188
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:20,000
Saying goodbye to today always feels like a loss

189
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:27,820
Look, tomorrow waves to me on the horizon

190
00:10:27,820 --> 00:10:35,440
Every day from sunrise to sunset, spinning time, dreaming more

191
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:40,500
Treasure every second, every moment in life

192
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:47,220
Bright eyes are sparkling

193
00:10:47,220 --> 00:10:50,600
A smile that faces the sun

194
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:55,820
It doesn't quietly linger at the blinking crossroad